  "meta": {
    "title": "Why the USA Planted a Wall of Trees From Canada to Texas 🌳🇺🇸😱",
    "description": "In the 1930s the Great Plains 🇺🇸 were hit by the Dust Bowl: giant dust storms blew away farmland 🌪️ So in 1934 President Franklin D. Roosevelt launched the Great Plains Shelterbelt 🌳 By 1942, 220 million trees had been planted in a 100-mile-wide zone from the Canadian border in North Dakota to Texas, forming 30,233 shelterbelts to slow the wind and keep moisture in the soil 💧",
    "pinnedComment": [
      "220 million trees to stop the wind 🌳🤯",
      "Have you ever seen a shelterbelt? 👇",
      "Which giant project should we explain next? 🗺️"
    ],
